      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`Optional[str]` can be written in two equivalent schema spellings, and `K2V3Detector` gets a different case wrong for each:\n\n| schema | untyped XML value `123` | explicit null (JSON `null`, or `arg_type` `null`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `{\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}` (Pydantic's default for `Optional[str]`) | `123` (int), expected `\"123\"` | `null` (correct) |\n| `{\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}` | `\"123\"` (correct) | `\"null\"` (string), expected `null` |\n\nCauses:\n- `_argument_type` returns `None` for any `anyOf`/`oneOf`, so the value falls through to best-effort `json.loads`. The `type`-list path already narrows `[X, \"null\"]` to `X`.\n- `_coerce_value` coerces an explicit null to the schema type. For `string` this means `json.dumps(None)`, which gives `\"null\"`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `_argument_type`: an `anyOf`/`oneOf` with exactly one non-null branch (after resolving local `$ref`) uses that branch's type, matching the `type`-list handling. Real multi-branch unions still return `None`, so the wire `arg_type` keeps precedence. `test_xml_typed_union_uses_wire_value_type` is unchanged and still passes.\n- `_coerce_value`: an explicit null (JSON `null` or `arg_type` `null`) is returned as `None` before any schema coercion.\n- Added `test_optional_string_keeps_text_and_null` to `test_k2_v3_detector.py`. All three sub-cases fail on current main.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A: parser-only change, covered by unit tests.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] `pytest test/registered/unit/function_call` passes (639 passed)\n- [x] pre-commit passes\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40303691568](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40303691568)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40303691572](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40303691572)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40303691585](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40303691585)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
